# Working conversions from the RFC-0001 exercise: existing crawlers expressed in the format by
# hand, before any interpreter existed. They found the revisions recorded in the RFC and that was
# their purpose.
#
# Not committed, deliberately. None of them was ever run, so every selector is a claim, and they are
# shaped exactly like real specs while being excluded from CI. Committed they would rot against a
# format that changed twenty-two times while they were written, and someone would copy a selector
# out of one.
#
# Kept on disk because they are still the fastest way to check whether a format change breaks
# something real.
drafts/
